# ArCoN v3.0 package catalog
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One logical package per line, pipe separated. Columns:
#   id | groups | arch | debian | ubuntu | fedora | opensuse | brew | winget | flatpak | description
#
#   "-"          not available / not applicable on that platform
#   arch         v2.5 native name; ArCoN decides pacman vs AUR at runtime
#                exactly like v2.5 did (pacman -Si hit => official, else AUR)
#   brew         "cask:NAME" for casks, plain NAME for formulae
#   flatpak      Flathub application id (Linux fallback, opt-in: PKG_ALLOW_FLATPAK)
#   groups       comma separated; v2.5 groups: essentials media cyber remote power
#                internal groups (used by modules): gaming gpu security hardened
#                shell terminal hyprland gnome base optimize
#
# Every non "-" cell is validated by scripts/verify-catalog.py against the
# official package indexes (see docs/PACKAGE-CATALOG.md for the last report).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
